[{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Tutorial","page":"Tutorial","text":"","title":"Tutorial"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Storage-and-geometry","page":"Tutorial","text":"A Paramorph declaration keeps ordinary Julia storage types intact and places the constraint after a tilde:\n\n@paramorph T struct Scale{T<:Real}\n    value::T ~ TV.asℝ₊\n    label::String = \"default\"\nend\n\ns = Scale{Float64}(2.0, \"custom\")\nθ = unconstrain(s)\nconstraint(s, θ)\nMain.Scale{Float64}(2.0, \"custom\")\n\nlabel has no ~, so it is auxiliary and does not consume optimizer coordinates. Structs with auxiliary fields intentionally do not receive an inferred unparameterized outer constructor: use the fully parameterized constructor, as above, or define a domain-specific outer constructor.\n\nType-based reconstruction is possible when geometry is determined entirely by the type:\n\nconstraint(Scale{Float64}, [0.0])\nMain.Scale{Float64}(1.0, \"default\")\n\nThe auxiliary default is used because there is no prototype from which to copy label.","title":"Storage and geometry"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Geometry-depending-on-runtime-fields","page":"Tutorial","text":"Transformation expressions may refer directly to fields:\n\n@paramorph T struct Weights{T<:Real}\n    n::Int\n    value::Vector{T} ~ TV.UnitSimplex(n)\nend\n\nw = Weights{Float64}(3, [0.2, 0.3, 0.5])\nintrinsic_dimension(w)\nconstraint(w, zeros(2))\nMain.Weights{Float64}(3, [0.3333333333333333, 0.33333333333333337, 0.33333333333333337])\n\nHere n is only stored at runtime, so Weights{Float64} cannot by itself identify a parameter space. Use a prototype object for constraint and intrinsic_dimension, or pass the auxiliary field explicitly to type-based operations.","title":"Geometry depending on runtime fields"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Type-dependent-geometry","page":"Tutorial","text":"A type parameter may be referenced without requiring a prototype:\n\n@paramorph T struct FixedWeights{N,T<:Real}\n    value::Vector{T} ~ TV.UnitSimplex(N)\nend\n\nintrinsic_dimension(FixedWeights{4,Float64})\n3","title":"Type-dependent geometry"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Nested-parameterizations-and-context","page":"Tutorial","text":"Nested parameterization is explicit through nested. Keyword arguments form a local context visible in the child declaration:\n\n@paramorph T struct Child{T<:Real}\n    θ::T ~ closed_lower(get(context, :lower, zero(T)))\nend\n\n@paramorph T struct Parent{D,T<:Real}\n    child::Child{T} ~ nested(lower=-inv(T(D - 1)))\nend\n\np = constraint(Parent{3,Float64}, [0.0])\np.child.θ\n0.5\n\nThis keeps parent-dependent constraints next to the field declaration instead of requiring external schema_context methods.\n\nFor homogeneous vectors of Paramorph objects use recursive:\n\n@paramorph T struct Forest{N,T<:Real}\n    children::Vector{Child{T}} ~ recursive(N; lower=zero(T))\nend\n\nintrinsic_dimension(Forest{2,Float64})\n2","title":"Nested parameterizations and context"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Coupled-fields","page":"Tutorial","text":"Some geometries are genuinely joint rather than Cartesian products of field constraints. Use one @geometry declaration inside the struct:\n\nfunction ordered_pair_transform()\n    base = TV.as((lower=TV.asℝ, gap=TV.asℝ₊))\n    forward = p -> (; lower=p.lower, upper=p.lower + p.gap)\n    backward = p -> (; lower=p.lower, gap=p.upper - p.lower)\n    joint_transform(base, forward, backward)\nend\n\n@paramorph T struct OrderedPair{T<:Real}\n    lower::T\n    upper::T\n    @geometry ((lower, upper) ~ ordered_pair_transform())\nend\n\npair = OrderedPair(0.0, 2.0)\nunconstrain(pair)\nconstraint(OrderedPair{Float64}, zeros(2))\nMain.OrderedPair{Float64}(0.0, 1.0)\n\nThe transformation must use a named tuple with the fields listed in @geometry. Field-level ~ declarations and @geometry intentionally cannot be mixed in the same struct.","title":"Coupled fields"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Custom-transforms-need-no-registration","page":"Tutorial","text":"Because the storage type is explicit, Paramorph does not need a registry that knows the output type of every transformation:\n\n@paramorph T struct MyModel{T<:Real}\n    parameter::Vector{T} ~ my_custom_transform()\nend\n\nIf my_custom_transform() satisfies the TransformVariables transformation interface and produces a value compatible with Vector{T}, no Paramorph method is required.","title":"Custom transforms need no registration"},{"category":"section","location":"#Paramorph.jl","page":"Home","text":"Paramorph declares how the parameter fields of an immutable Julia struct map to flat unconstrained coordinates.\n\nThe 0.0.3 DSL has one central rule:\n\nfield::StorageType ~ geometry\n\n:: describes storage. ~ describes parameter geometry. Fields without ~ are auxiliary.\n\nSee the tutorial for field-dependent geometry, nested structs and coupled parameterizations.","title":"Paramorph.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Core-interface","page":"Home","text":"The core interface consists of the declaration macro and the coordinate operations described throughout the tutorial:\n\n@paramorph T struct Model{T<:Real}\n    parameter::T ~ transform\nend\n\nintrinsic_dimension(model)\nθ = unconstrain(model)\nmodel′ = constraint(model, θ)\nmodel′, logjac = constraint_with_logjac(model, θ)\n\nconstraint(Type, θ) is also available when the parameter geometry is fully determined by the type. If a transformation expression depends on runtime fields, use a prototype object instead.\n\nnested(; context...) makes a nested @paramorph field part of the same parameterization and forwards a local context. recursive([count]; context...) does the same for recursive containers.","title":"Core interface"},{"category":"section","location":"#Documented-building-blocks","page":"Home","text":"positive_vector_with_sum_below and asymmetric_mixed are also exported specialized transforms; their motivation and use are illustrated by the model packages that need them.","title":"Documented building blocks"},{"category":"macro","location":"#Paramorph.@paramorph","page":"Home","text":"@paramorph T struct Model{...,T<:Real,...}\n    parameter::StorageType ~ geometry\n    auxiliary::OtherType\nend\n\nAttach a Paramorph parameter geometry to an immutable Julia struct. The storage annotation after :: is ordinary Julia; the expression after ~ is the unconstrained-coordinate geometry for that field. Fields without ~ are auxiliary and are excluded from the parameter vector.\n\nGeometry expressions may reference type parameters, context, and fields of the struct. Geometry depending on constrained parameter values requires a prototype; geometry depending only on auxiliary fields can be supplied to type-based operations with auxiliary=(; field=value, ...).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.@paramorph"},{"category":"function","location":"#Paramorph.closed_lower","page":"Home","text":"closed_lower(lower) creates a lower-bounded transform whose inverse accepts the boundary.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.closed_lower"},{"category":"function","location":"#Paramorph.open_lower","page":"Home","text":"open_lower(lower) creates a strictly lower-bounded transform (lower, ∞).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.open_lower"},{"category":"function","location":"#Paramorph.nonnegative","page":"Home","text":"nonnegative() creates a transform to the closed nonnegative half-line.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.nonnegative"},{"category":"function","location":"#Paramorph.bounded_interval","page":"Home","text":"bounded_interval(lower, upper; left_closed=true, right_closed=true) creates an interval transform.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.bounded_interval"},{"category":"function","location":"#Paramorph.correlation_matrix","page":"Home","text":"correlation_matrix(n) transforms coordinates into an n × n correlation matrix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.correlation_matrix"},{"category":"function","location":"#Paramorph.closed_correlation_matrix","page":"Home","text":"closed_correlation_matrix(n) transforms coordinates into an n × n correlation matrix, including boundaries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.closed_correlation_matrix"},{"category":"function","location":"#Paramorph.positive_definite_matrix","page":"Home","text":"positive_definite_matrix(n) transforms coordinates into an n × n SPD matrix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.positive_definite_matrix"},{"category":"function","location":"#Paramorph.variogram_matrix","page":"Home","text":"variogram_matrix(d) transforms coordinates into a strict d × d variogram.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.variogram_matrix"},{"category":"function","location":"#Paramorph.compact_variogram_matrix","page":"Home","text":"compact_variogram_matrix(d) transforms coordinates into a strict d × d variogram, including boundaries.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.compact_variogram_matrix"},{"category":"function","location":"#Paramorph.repeat_transform","page":"Home","text":"repeat_transform(inner, count) repeats a transformation and returns a vector of results.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.repeat_transform"},{"category":"function","location":"#Paramorph.joint_transform","page":"Home","text":"joint_transform(base, forward, backward; flatten=identity) defines a coupled bijection.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.joint_transform"},{"category":"function","location":"#Paramorph.polytope","page":"Home","text":"polytope(A, b; center=zeros(...))\n\nMap Euclidean coordinates bijectively to the interior of the bounded polytope A * y <= b, using radial projection from a strictly interior point. The map is piecewise smooth where the active facet changes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Paramorph.polytope"}]
